  "raw_text": "248\n\nTara pulan l\nâ\nka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nway of pretending to be important, way of acting important, self\n-\nimportance,\n\narrogance, pride\n \n/ forma de pretender ser importante, forma de actuar importante,\n \nimportancia\n\npersonal, arrogancia, orgullo\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb\n-\n07/20\n):\n \nFero ba tara pulan lâka brin sakuna ai dara walras kira Gâd kupia lâka aimakbia hilp munan\n\n–\n \nPharaoh had arrogance but unconsciously, he helped fulfill God’s will\n \n/ Faraón tenía arrogancia pero\n\ninconscientemente, ayudó\n \na que se cumpliera la voluntad de Dios\n)\n\nW\nî\nna tara\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nbody\n \n/ cuerpo\n\n(\nEx/\nEj\n(\nwqu\n-\n08/19\n):\n \nwan wîna tara karnika ba mâyara iwan sa kaka\n \n–\n \nif our physical strength has declined\n \n/ si nuestra\n\nfuerza física ha\n \ndisminuido\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb\n-\n05/21\n):\n \nMaya waitna latwankira kum wîna tara lainka ra bara spirit lainka ra ai pamalika dîa nit ba yabia\n \n–\n \nA\n\nloving husband will give his family what they need physically and spiritually\n \n/ Un esposo amoroso le dará a su\n \nfamilia lo\n\nque necesitan física y espiritualmente\n)\n\nW\nî\nna tara brinka saura nani\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nfleshly desires\n \n/ deseos carnales\n\nWîna tara yamnika\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ngood health, health\n \n/ buena salud, salud\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb-05/20\n):\n \nTuman lâka ba wan wîna tara yamnika sauhkisa.\n \n–\n \nJealousy harms our health.\n \n/ Los celos\ndañan nuestra salud.)\n\nTarka\n \n(adj,n/s)\n \n–\n \ngreatness, largeness, immensity, the greater part, the bigger part, superior, bigger\n \n/ grandeza,\namplitud, inmensidad, la mayor parte, superior, mayor\n\nBiara\n \ntarka\n \n(a/t:\n \nBiara tarkika\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nlarge intestine\n \n/ intestino grueso\n\nBila tarka\n \n–\n \nthe broad or wide part\n \n/ la parte ancha\n\nTarka tara\n \n(\nTarkatara\n-\nbh,sn\n)\n \n–\n \nvery big, huge, enormous\n \n/ muy grande, enorme\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nlfb54)\n:\n \nJehova inska tarka tara kum blikan Jona ra langkaia\n \n–\n \nJehovah sent an enormous fish to swallow Jonah\n \n/\nJehová envió un enorme pez para tragarse a Jonás)\n\nTarti\n \n(\nmba-\n \nfrom English / de inglés)\n \n–\n \nthirty\n \n/ treinta\n\nTartin\n \n(\nmba-\n \nfrom English / de inglés)\n \n–\n \nthirteen\n \n/ trece\n\nTasa\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nrubber\n \n/ hule\n\nTasba\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nearth, land, ground, soil, world\n \n/ tierra, suelo, mundo\n\n(Construct:\n \nTasbayi\n-db\n; Tasbaiam\n-\nmy51\n,\n \nTasbayam\n-\ndb\n;\n \nTasbaya\n-\ndb,lfb,wqu,mwb,km,fy,yc\n,\n \nTasbaia\n-\ndict,dba,bh,ks,my, lv,sn,sp\n,\n\nTasbaika\n-\ngf\n,\ndictu\n,\n \nTasbayka\n,\nTasbaya-\ndictu-alt\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej:\n \nTasba na bara diara nani bilara ba, latwan kaikpara\n \n–\n \nDo not love this world and the things within\n \n/ No ames este mundo y\nlas cosas dentro)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nlfb88\n):\n \nWitin nani ai ninara wih bara tasba ra kauhan\n \n–\n \nThey, going backward, fell to the ground\n \n/ Ellos, retrocediendo,\ncayeron al suelo)\n\nPramis tasbaya\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nPromised Land\n \n/\n \nT\nierra\n \nP\nrometida\n\nTasba bani\n \n–\n \nall the earth\n \n/ toda la tierra\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\ndb\n-\nSins L\nâ\nka\n \n15:3\n):\n \nTasba bani ra, Dawan nakra b\nâ\nra sa\n \n–\n \nIn all the\n \nearth, God’s eyes are there\n \n/ En toda la tierra, los\n\nojos de Dios están ahí)\n\nTasba brinka\n \n–\n \nearthly desire\n \n/ deseo terrenal\n\nTasba dukya nani latwanka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nmaterialism\n \n/ materialismo\n\nTasba gabamintka\n \n–\n \nhuman government\n \n/ gobierno humano\n\nTasba lukanka nani\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nworld’s thoughts, world’s ideas, world’s thinking\n \n/ pensamientos del mundo, ideas del\nmundo, pensamiento del mundo\n\nTasba nikban\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nearthquake\n \n/ terremoto\n\n(Ex/Ej(\ndb-Matiu 24:7\n):\n \ntasba nikban nani sin plis ailal ra kabia\n \n–\n \nalso there will be earthquakes in many places\n \n/ también\nhabrá terremotos en muchos lugares)\n\nTasba ra iwaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto live on earth\n \n/ vivir en la tierra\n\n(Ex/Ej:\n \ntasba ra iwaia bîla kaiki nani ba\n \n–\n \nthose hoping to live on earth\n \n/ aquellos que esperan vivir en la tierra)\n\nTasba raya\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nnew earth\n \n/ nueva tierra\n\nTasba sauhkanka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nnatural disaster\n \n/ desastre natural\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb-05/20\n):\n \nYawan sut dîa sip ba kat daukaia sa, tasba sauhkanka kum kau balras kainara ridi kaia dukiara.\n \n–\n \nWe\nmust do all that we are able to do in order to be ready before a natural disaster comes.\n \n/ Debemos hacer todo lo que\npodamos para estar preparados antes de que ocurra un desastre natural.)",
